  "texto": "If someone's done this to you — it wasn't an accident. It has a name. And there are 5 of them. Therapists see these exact 5 patterns in almost every toxic relationship. Recognize even ONE, and you'll never call it 'love' again. Number one: gaslighting. They make you doubt your own memory. Your own eyes. 'That never happened.' 'You're overreacting.' 'You're crazy.' It's not confusion. It's control. Number two: love bombing. Too much, too fast. Gifts, texts, 'soulmate' — in week one. It's not passion. It's a hook. The faster it starts, the harder it can trap you. Number three: the silent treatment. Not space. A punishment. They go cold on purpose — until you apologize for THEIR mistake. Silence, weaponized. Number four: guilt-tripping. 'After everything I've done for you...' Turning your needs into your fault. If you feel guilty for having limits — that's the tactic working. Number five: moving the goalposts. You finally do what they asked. Suddenly, it's not enough. The target keeps moving — so you can never win. That's the point. You're not supposed to win. Once you can name it... ...it loses its power over you. This isn't love. It's a playbook. And now you've read it. Comment the NUMBER that hit hardest. And send this to someone stuck in one of these.",
  "voz": "en-US-JennyNeural"
}